{
  "analysis": "The program compiles with only warnings (no errors) and is 4980 bytes, under the 5000 limit. However, I found a critical offset bug: the MLP c_fc weight and mlp c_proj weight/bias offsets use `P+5*H` but should use `P+4*H+M` because c_fc/bias has M=3072 elements, not H=768. I also have an extra `'m` contraction not in the real GPT-2 regex. I need fix these, recompile, and test.",
  "plan": "Use sed to replace `P+5*H` with `P+4*H+M` and remove the erroneous `'m` contraction. Then check source size, recompile, and run test prompts like \"Hello\" and \"The capital of France is\".",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -i 's/P+5\\*H/P+4*H+M/g' /app/gpt2.c\nsed -i 's/||s\\[i+1\\]==109//g' /app/gpt2.c\nwc -c /app/gpt2.c\ngcc -O3 -Wall /app/gpt2.c -o /app/a.out -lm 2>&1 | head -10\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "/app/a.out /app/gpt2-124M.ckpt /app/vocab.bpe \"Hello\"\n",
